/-!
# Integral closure and normality of semigroup algebras

Let `S` be a finitely generated additive submonoid of a torsion-free abelian group `G`, and let
`L_S = AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)` be the subgroup generated by `S`. Saturating `S` inside
`L_S` produces the submonoid
`S_sat = S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid`, whose generated
subgroup is again `L_S`, so the fraction rings of `R[S]`, `R[S_sat]`, and `R[L_S]` coincide
without enlarging the lattice (`AddMonoidAlgebra.isFractionRing_groupClosure` and
`AddMonoidAlgebra.isFractionRing_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure`).

This file establishes the ring-theoretic normalization theory of `R[S]`:
* **Descent to coefficients and Laurent polynomial normality**: if `R[M]` is integrally closed for
  any commutative monoid `M`, then `R` is integrally closed by faithfully flat descent
  (`AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_of_addMonoidAlgebra`, via
  `TauCeti.IsIntegrallyClosed.of_faithfullyFlat`); conversely, over an integrally closed domain `R`,
  the group algebra `R[G]` of any free abelian group `G` is integrally closed
  (`AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_of_free`).
* **Integral closure in `R[L_S]` and in `Frac(R[S])`**: transporting
  `AddSubmonoid.isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation` to the free lattice `L_S` identifies `R[S_sat]`
  with the integral closure of `R[S]` inside `R[L_S]` over any reduced ring `R`
  (`AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure`), and with the integral closure
  of `R[S]` inside any fraction ring `K` of `R[S]` over any integrally closed domain `R`
  (`AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_fractionRing` and
  `AddMonoidAlgebra.nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure`), yielding `Module.Finite` of
  those integral closures over `R[S]`
  (`AddMonoidAlgebra.moduleFinite_integralClosure_of_free`,
  `AddMonoidAlgebra.moduleFinite_integralClosure_addSubgroupClosure`, and
  `AddMonoidAlgebra.moduleFinite_integralClosure_fractionRing`).
* **Normality criterion**: over an integral domain `R` (or directly an integrally closed domain `R`,
  such as a field or `ℤ`), `R[S]` is integrally closed if and only if `R` is integrally closed and
  `S` is saturated in `L_S`
  (`AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_iff_isIntegrallyClosed_and_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq`,
  `AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_iff_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq_of_isIntegrallyClosed`,
  and `AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_of_nsmulSaturated`).

## Main declarations

* `AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_of_addMonoidAlgebra`: `IsIntegrallyClosed (R[M])` descends
  to `IsIntegrallyClosed R`.
* `AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_of_free`: `R[G]` is integrally closed when `R` is an
  integrally closed domain and `G` is `ℤ`-free.
* `AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure`: `R[S_sat]` is the integral
  closure of `R[S]` inside `R[L_S]` over any reduced ring `R`.
* `AddMonoidAlgebra.moduleFinite_integralClosure_of_free`,
  `AddMonoidAlgebra.moduleFinite_integralClosure_addSubgroupClosure`, and
  `AddMonoidAlgebra.moduleFinite_integralClosure_fractionRing`: finiteness of the integral closure
  of `R[S]` in `R[L]`, `R[L_S]`, and any fraction ring `K` of `R[S]`.
* `AddMonoidAlgebra.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing` and
  `AddMonoidAlgebra.isFractionRing_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure`: canonical embedding of `R[S_sat]`
  into any fraction ring `K` of `R[S]` (extending `AddMonoidAlgebra.groupClosureToFractionRing`),
  making `K` a fraction ring of `R[S_sat]`.
* `AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_fractionRing` and
  `AddMonoidAlgebra.nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure`: `R[S_sat]` is the integral
  closure of `R[S]` in any fraction ring `K` over an integrally closed domain `R`.
* `AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_of_nsmulSaturated_of_free`,
  `AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_nsmulSaturation`,
  `AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_of_nsmulSaturated`,
  `AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_iff_isIntegrallyClosed_and_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq`,
  and
  `AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_iff_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq_of_isIntegrallyClosed`:
  normality of saturated and saturation algebras, and normality of `R[S]` if and only if `S` is
  saturated inside `L_S` (and `R` is integrally closed).

## References

* W. Bruns and J. Gubeladze, *Polytopes, Rings, and K-Theory*, Chapters 2 and 4 (Theorem 4.40).
* W. Bruns and J. Herzog, *Cohen–Macaulay Rings*, §6.1 (Theorem 6.1.4).
* W. Fulton, *Introduction to Toric Varieties*, §§1.2 and 2.1.
* D. Cox, J. Little and H. Schenck, *Toric Varieties*, §1.2 and §1.3 (Theorem 1.3.5).
-/

public section

open scoped nonZeroDivisors

namespace AddMonoidAlgebra

section CoeffAndFreeGroup

/-- If the monoid algebra `R[M]` of a commutative monoid `M` is integrally closed, then the
coefficient ring `R` is integrally closed. -/
theorem isIntegrallyClosed_of_addMonoidAlgebra {R M : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommMonoid M]
    [IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R M)] : IsIntegrallyClosed R := by
  have : Module.FaithfullyFlat R (AddMonoidAlgebra R M) :=
    .of_linearEquiv R (M →₀ R) (coeffLinearEquiv R)
  exact TauCeti.IsIntegrallyClosed.of_faithfullyFlat R (AddMonoidAlgebra R M)

/-- Over an integrally closed domain `R`, the group algebra `R[G]` of any free abelian group `G`
is integrally closed. -/
instance isIntegrallyClosed_of_free {R G : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R]
    [AddCommGroup G] [Module.Free ℤ G] : IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R G) := by
  let b := Module.Free.chooseBasis ℤ G
  let ι := Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex ℤ G
  refine IsIntegrallyClosed.of_equiv (mapDomainRingEquiv R b.repr.toAddEquiv).symm (h := ?_)
  let j : (ι →₀ ℕ) →+ (ι →₀ ℤ) := Finsupp.mapRange.addMonoidHom (Nat.castAddMonoidHom ℤ)
  have hj : Function.Injective j :=
    Finsupp.mapRange_injective _ Nat.cast_zero Nat.cast_injective
  let P : AddSubmonoid (ι →₀ ℤ) := AddMonoidHom.mrange j
  have hP_top : AddSubgroup.closure (P : Set (ι →₀ ℤ)) = ⊤ := by
    rw [eq_top_iff]
    intro v _
    let vPos : ι →₀ ℕ := v.mapRange Int.toNat rfl
    let vNeg : ι →₀ ℕ := (-v).mapRange Int.toNat rfl
    have hv : v = j vPos - j vNeg := by
      ext i
      simp [j, vPos, vNeg]
    rw [hv]
    exact sub_mem (AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨vPos, rfl⟩) (AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨vNeg, rfl⟩)
  let eP : (ι →₀ ℕ) ≃+ P := AddEquiv.ofBijective (j.codRestrict P fun x => ⟨x, rfl⟩)
    ⟨(j.injective_codRestrict P _).mpr hj, fun ⟨_, x, rfl⟩ => ⟨x, rfl⟩⟩
  have hIC_mv : IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R (ι →₀ ℕ)) :=
    TauCeti.MvPolynomial.isIntegrallyClosed (σ := ι) (R := R)
  have hIC_P : IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R P) :=
    IsIntegrallyClosed.of_equiv (mapDomainRingEquiv R eP) (h := hIC_mv)
  let := (mapDomainRingHom R P.toGroupClosure).toAlgebra
  have := P.isLocalization_addMonoidAlgebra_groupClosure R
  have hIC_cl : IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R (AddSubgroup.closure (P : Set (ι →₀ ℤ)))) :=
    isIntegrallyClosed_of_isLocalization _ (MonoidHom.mrange (of R P)) mrange_of_le_nonZeroDivisors
  exact IsIntegrallyClosed.of_equiv
    (mapDomainRingEquiv R ((AddEquiv.addSubgroupCongr hP_top).trans AddSubgroup.topEquiv))
    (h := hIC_cl)

end CoeffAndFreeGroup

section GroupClosure

/-- For a finitely generated submonoid `S` of a free abelian group `L` and any reduced commutative
ring `R`, the integral closure of `R[S]` inside `R[L]` is a finite `R[S]`-module. -/
theorem moduleFinite_integralClosure_of_free {R L : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsReduced R]
    [AddCommGroup L] [Module.Free ℤ L] {S : AddSubmonoid L} (hS : S.FG) :
    letI := (mapDomainRingHom R S.subtype).toAlgebra
    Module.Finite (AddMonoidAlgebra R S)
      (integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L)) := by
  let _ : Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R S.nsmulSaturation) :=
    (mapDomainRingHom R (AddSubmonoid.inclusion S.le_nsmulSaturation)).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L) :=
    (mapDomainRingHom R S.subtype).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S.nsmulSaturation) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L) :=
    (mapDomainRingHom R S.nsmulSaturation.subtype).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R S.nsmulSaturation)
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R L) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun f => by
      simp only [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra, ← RingHom.comp_apply, ← mapDomainRingHom_comp,
        AddSubmonoid.subtype_comp_inclusion]
  have : IsIntegralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S.nsmulSaturation) (AddMonoidAlgebra R S)
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R L) := S.isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation R
  have : Module.Finite (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R S.nsmulSaturation) :=
    TauCeti.AddMonoidAlgebra.mapDomainRingHom_inclusion_nsmulSaturation_finite hS R
  exact Module.Finite.equiv
    (IsIntegralClosure.equiv (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R S.nsmulSaturation)
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R L)
      (integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L))).toLinearEquiv

/-- **Integral closure inside `R[L_S]`.** For any finitely generated submonoid `S` of a
torsion-free abelian group `G` and any reduced commutative ring `R`, the algebra of
`S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid` is the integral closure of
`R[S]` inside `R[AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)]`. -/
theorem isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure {R G : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsReduced R] [AddCommGroup G] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG) :
    letI := (mapDomainRingHom R S.toGroupClosure).toAlgebra
    letI := (mapDomainRingHom R S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure).toAlgebra
    IsIntegralClosure
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid))
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R S)
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G))) := by
  -- Transport `AddSubmonoid.isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation` from `S₀ ≤ L_S` to `S` and `S_sat`.
  set L_S := AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)
  set S₀ := S.comap L_S.subtype
  have : L_S.FG := hS.addSubgroupClosure
  let _ : Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S₀) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L_S) :=
    (mapDomainRingHom R S₀.subtype).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S₀.nsmulSaturation) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L_S) :=
    (mapDomainRingHom R S₀.nsmulSaturation.subtype).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L_S) :=
    (mapDomainRingHom R S.toGroupClosure).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ L_S.toAddSubmonoid))
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R L_S) :=
    (mapDomainRingHom R S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure).toAlgebra
  have h₁ : (S.toGroupClosure : S → L_S) ∘ S.toGroupClosureEquiv.symm = S₀.subtype :=
    funext fun _ => by simp
  have h₂ : (S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure : _ → L_S) ∘
      S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquiv.symm = S₀.nsmulSaturation.subtype :=
    funext fun _ => by simp
  refine (S₀.isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation R).of_ringEquiv
    (mapDomainRingEquiv R S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquiv.symm)
    (mapDomainRingEquiv R S.toGroupClosureEquiv.symm) (.refl _)
    (fun r => by simp only [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra, RingEquiv.coe_refl, id_eq,
      mapDomainRingHom_apply, mapDomainRingEquiv_eq_mapDomain, mapDomain_mapDomain, h₁])
    (fun a => by simp only [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra, RingEquiv.coe_refl, id_eq,
      mapDomainRingHom_apply, mapDomainRingEquiv_eq_mapDomain, mapDomain_mapDomain, h₂])

/-- For any finitely generated submonoid `S` of a torsion-free abelian group `G` and any reduced
commutative ring `R`, the integral closure of `R[S]` inside `R[AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)]` is
a finite `R[S]`-module. -/
theorem moduleFinite_integralClosure_addSubgroupClosure {R G : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsReduced R]
    [AddCommGroup G] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG) :
    letI := (mapDomainRingHom R S.toGroupClosure).toAlgebra
    Module.Finite (AddMonoidAlgebra R S)
      (integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S)
        (AddMonoidAlgebra R (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)))) := by
  set L_S := AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)
  set S_sat := S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ L_S.toAddSubmonoid
  let _ : Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R S_sat) :=
    (mapDomainRingHom R
      (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure))).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L_S) :=
    (mapDomainRingHom R S.toGroupClosure).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S_sat) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L_S) :=
    (mapDomainRingHom R S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R S_sat) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L_S) :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun f => by
      simp only [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra, ← RingHom.comp_apply, ← mapDomainRingHom_comp,
        S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure_comp_inclusion]
  have : IsIntegralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S_sat) (AddMonoidAlgebra R S)
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R L_S) := isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure hS
  have : Module.Finite (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R S_sat) :=
    TauCeti.AddMonoidAlgebra.mapDomainRingHom_inclusion_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_finite hS R
  exact Module.Finite.equiv
    (IsIntegralClosure.equiv (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R S_sat)
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R L_S)
      (integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L_S))).toLinearEquiv

end GroupClosure

section FractionFieldAndNormality

variable {G : Type*} [AddCommGroup G]

/-- The canonical ring homomorphism from the algebra of the saturation of `S` inside
`AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)` into any fraction ring `K` of `R[S]`. -/
noncomputable def nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing (S : AddSubmonoid G) (R K : Type*)
    [CommRing R] [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] :
    AddMonoidAlgebra R ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid) →+*
      K :=
  (groupClosureToFractionRing S R K).comp
    (mapDomainRingHom R S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure)

/-- `nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing` is the composite of `groupClosureToFractionRing` with
`mapDomainRingHom R S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure`. -/
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_def (S : AddSubmonoid G) (R K : Type*) [CommRing R]
    [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] :
    nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K =
      (groupClosureToFractionRing S R K).comp
        (mapDomainRingHom R S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure) :=
  (rfl)

/-- `nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing` factors through `groupClosureToFractionRing` along
`S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure`. -/
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_apply (S : AddSubmonoid G) (R K : Type*)
    [CommRing R] [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    (f : AddMonoidAlgebra R
      ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid)) :
    nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K f =
      groupClosureToFractionRing S R K
        (mapDomain S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure f) :=
  (rfl)

/-- Composing `nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing` with the `mapDomainRingHom` induced by the
inclusion of `S` into its saturation inside `AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)` recovers
`algebraMap (R[S]) K`. -/
@[simp]
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_comp_mapDomainRingHom_inclusion
    (S : AddSubmonoid G) (R K : Type*) [CommRing R] [CommRing K]
    [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] :
    (nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K).comp
        (mapDomainRingHom R
          (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure))) =
      algebraMap (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K := by
  rw [nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_def, RingHom.comp_assoc, ← mapDomainRingHom_comp,
    S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure_comp_inclusion,
    groupClosureToFractionRing_comp_mapDomainRingHom_toGroupClosure]

/-- `nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing` extends `algebraMap (R[S]) K` along the inclusion of
`S` into its saturation inside `AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_mapDomain_inclusion (S : AddSubmonoid G)
    (R K : Type*) [CommRing R] [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] (f : AddMonoidAlgebra R S) :
    nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K
        (mapDomain
          (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure)) f) =
      algebraMap (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K f := by
  rw [nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_apply, mapDomain_mapDomain, ← AddMonoidHom.coe_comp,
    S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure_comp_inclusion,
    groupClosureToFractionRing_mapDomain_toGroupClosure]

/-- `nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing` maps a monomial from `S` to its image under
`algebraMap (R[S]) K`. -/
@[simp]
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_single_inclusion (S : AddSubmonoid G)
    (R K : Type*) [CommRing R] [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] (s : S) (r : R) :
    nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K
        (single (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure) s)
          r) =
      algebraMap (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K (single s r) := by
  rw [← mapDomain_single, nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_mapDomain_inclusion]

/-- `nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing` maps a constant monomial `single 0 r` to its image
under `algebraMap (R[S]) K`. -/
@[simp]
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_single_zero (S : AddSubmonoid G) (R K : Type*)
    [CommRing R] [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] (r : R) :
    nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K (single 0 r) =
      algebraMap (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K (single 0 r) := by
  simp [nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_apply]

/-- `nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing` maps a general saturation monomial `single x r` to the
image of `single (S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure x) r` under
`groupClosureToFractionRing`. -/
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_single (S : AddSubmonoid G) (R K : Type*)
    [CommRing R] [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    (x : ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid)) (r : R) :
    nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K (single x r) =
      groupClosureToFractionRing S R K
        (single (S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure x) r) := by
  rw [nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_apply, mapDomain_single]

/-- When a saturation element `x` decomposes as `a - b` in `G` with `a b : S`,
`nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing` evaluates `single x r` as the fraction
`single a r / single b 1` in `K`. -/
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_single_eq_mk'_of_coe_eq_sub (S : AddSubmonoid G)
    (R K : Type*) [CommRing R] [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    {x : ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid)} {a b : S}
    (hx : (x : G) = a - b) (r : R) :
    nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K (single x r) =
      IsLocalization.mk' K (single a r) ⟨single b 1, single_mem_nonZeroDivisors b (one_mem _)⟩ := by
  rw [nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_single]
  have hsub : S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure x =
      S.toGroupClosure a - S.toGroupClosure b :=
    Subtype.ext (by simpa using hx)
  rw [hsub, groupClosureToFractionRing_single_sub_toGroupClosure]

/-- `nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing` is injective. -/
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_injective (S : AddSubmonoid G) (R K : Type*)
    [CommRing R] [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] :
    Function.Injective (nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K) :=
  (groupClosureToFractionRing_injective S R K).comp
    (mapDomain_injective S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure_injective)

/-- For any commutative ring `R`, any fraction ring `K` of `R[S]` is also a fraction ring of
`R[S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid]` along
`nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing`. -/
theorem isFractionRing_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure (S : AddSubmonoid G) (R K : Type*) [CommRing R]
    [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] :
    letI := (nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K).toAlgebra
    IsFractionRing
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid))
      K := by
  set S_sat := S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid
  let B := AddMonoidAlgebra R S_sat
  let C₀ := AddMonoidAlgebra R (AddSubgroup.closure (S_sat : Set G))
  let C := AddMonoidAlgebra R (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G))
  let _ : Algebra B C₀ := (mapDomainRingHom R S_sat.toGroupClosure).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra B C := (mapDomainRingHom R S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra C K := (groupClosureToFractionRing S R K).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra B K := (nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower B C K := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun f =>
    (nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_apply S R K f).symm
  have := S_sat.isLocalization_addMonoidAlgebra_groupClosure R
  let e : C₀ ≃ₐ[B] C :=
    AlgEquiv.ofRingEquiv
      (f := mapDomainRingEquiv R
        (AddEquiv.addSubgroupCongr S.addSubgroupClosure_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure))
      fun f => by
        have hcomp :
            ((AddEquiv.addSubgroupCongr S.addSubgroupClosure_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure :
                AddSubgroup.closure (S_sat : Set G) → _) ∘
              S_sat.toGroupClosure) = S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure :=
          funext fun _ => Subtype.ext (by simp)
        rw [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra, RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra,
          mapDomainRingEquiv_eq_mapDomain, mapDomainRingHom_apply, mapDomainRingHom_apply,
          mapDomain_mapDomain, hcomp]
  have : IsLocalization (MonoidHom.mrange (of R S_sat)) C :=
    IsLocalization.isLocalization_of_algEquiv (MonoidHom.mrange (of R S_sat)) e
  have : IsFractionRing C K := isFractionRing_groupClosure S R K
  exact TauCeti.IsFractionRing.of_isLocalization_of_isFractionRing
    (MonoidHom.mrange (of R S_sat)) C K mrange_of_le_nonZeroDivisors

/-- **Integral closure of `R[S]` in its own fraction ring.** Over an integrally closed domain `R`,
for any finitely generated submonoid `S` of a torsion-free abelian group `G` and any fraction ring
`K` of `R[S]`, the algebra `R[S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure S).toAddSubmonoid]` is the
integral closure of `R[S]` in `K`. -/
theorem isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_fractionRing {R K : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG)
    [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] :
    letI := (nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K).toAlgebra
    IsIntegralClosure
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid))
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K := by
  set A := AddMonoidAlgebra R S
  set B :=
    AddMonoidAlgebra R ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid)
  set C := AddMonoidAlgebra R (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G))
  let _ : Algebra A C := (mapDomainRingHom R S.toGroupClosure).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra B C := (mapDomainRingHom R S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureToGroupClosure).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra C K := (groupClosureToFractionRing S R K).toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra B K := (nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower A C K := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun f =>
    (groupClosureToFractionRing_mapDomain_toGroupClosure S R K f).symm
  have : IsScalarTower B C K := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun f =>
    (nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_apply S R K f).symm
  have : IsFractionRing C K := isFractionRing_groupClosure S R K
  have := hS.addSubgroupClosure
  have : IsIntegrallyClosedIn C K :=
    (isIntegrallyClosed_iff_isIntegrallyClosedIn K).mp inferInstance
  have : IsIntegralClosure B A C := isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure hS
  exact IsIntegralClosure.of_isIntegralClosure_of_isIntegrallyClosedIn A B C K

/-- Over an integrally closed domain `R`, for any finitely generated submonoid `S` of a
torsion-free abelian group `G`, the image of `nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing` in any
fraction ring `K` of `R[S]` equals the integral closure of `R[S]` in `K`. -/
theorem range_nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing {R K : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG) [CommRing K]
    [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] :
    (nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K).range =
      (integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K).toSubring := by
  let := (nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K).toAlgebra
  have hIC := isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_fractionRing (R := R) hS (K := K)
  ext x
  exact hIC.isIntegral_iff.symm

/-- Over an integrally closed domain `R`, for a finitely generated submonoid `S` of a torsion-free
abelian group `G`, the canonical `R[S]`-algebra isomorphism between
`R[S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure S).toAddSubmonoid]` and the integral closure of `R[S]`
in any fraction ring `K` of `R[S]` (for instance `K = FractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S)`). -/
noncomputable def nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG)
    (K : Type*) [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] :
    letI := (mapDomainRingHom R
      (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure))).toAlgebra
    AddMonoidAlgebra R ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid) ≃ₐ[
        AddMonoidAlgebra R S]
      integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K :=
  letI := (mapDomainRingHom R
    (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure))).toAlgebra
  letI := (nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K).toAlgebra
  haveI : IsScalarTower (AddMonoidAlgebra R S)
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid))
      K :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun f =>
      (nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_mapDomain_inclusion S R K f).symm
  haveI := isIntegralClosure_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_fractionRing (R := R) hS (K := K)
  IsIntegralClosure.equiv (AddMonoidAlgebra R S)
    (AddMonoidAlgebra R ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid)) K
    (integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K)

/-- `nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure` acts on `K` via
`nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure_apply {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG)
    (K : Type*) [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    (f : AddMonoidAlgebra R
      ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid)) :
    (nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure hS K f : K) =
      nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K f := by
  have h :
      algebraMap (integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K) K
          (nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure hS K f) =
        nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K f := by
    rw [nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure, IsIntegralClosure.algebraMap_equiv,
      RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra]
  simpa using h

/-- `nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure` maps an element pushed forward from `R[S]`
along `AddSubmonoid.inclusion` to its `algebraMap` image in `integralClosure (R[S]) K`. -/
@[simp]
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure_mapDomain_inclusion {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG)
    (K : Type*) [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] (f : AddMonoidAlgebra R S) :
    nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure hS K
        (mapDomain
          (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure)) f) =
      algebraMap (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K) f := by
  ext
  simp

/-- `nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure` maps a monomial coming from `S` along
`AddSubmonoid.inclusion` to its `algebraMap` image in `integralClosure (R[S]) K`. -/
@[simp]
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure_single_inclusion {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG)
    (K : Type*) [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] (s : S) (r : R) :
    nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure hS K
        (single
          (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure) s) r) =
      algebraMap (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K)
        (single s r) := by
  rw [← mapDomain_single, nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure_mapDomain_inclusion]

/-- `nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure` maps a constant monomial `single 0 r` to its
`algebraMap` image in `integralClosure (R[S]) K`. -/
@[simp]
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure_single_zero {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG)
    (K : Type*) [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] (r : R) :
    nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure hS K (single 0 r) =
      algebraMap (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K)
        (single 0 r) := by
  ext
  simp

/-- Applying `nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing` to the inverse of
`nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure` recovers the underlying element of `K`. -/
@[simp]
theorem
    nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing_nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure_symm_apply
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G]
    {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG) (K : Type*) [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] (x : integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K) :
    letI := (mapDomainRingHom R
      (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure))).toAlgebra
    nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K
        ((nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure hS K).symm x) =
      x := by
  let := (mapDomainRingHom R
    (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure))).toAlgebra
  rw [← coe_nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure_apply hS K, AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]

/-- `(nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure hS K).symm` recovers `f` from its image under
`nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing`. -/
@[simp]
theorem nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure_symm_apply_mk {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG)
    (K : Type*) [CommRing K] [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K]
    (f : AddMonoidAlgebra R
      ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid))
    (hf : nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K f ∈
      integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K) :
    letI := (mapDomainRingHom R
      (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure))).toAlgebra
    (nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure hS K).symm
        ⟨nsmulSaturationInfClosureToFractionRing S R K f, hf⟩ =
      f := by
  let := (mapDomainRingHom R
    (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure))).toAlgebra
  apply (nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure hS K).injective
  ext
  simp

/-- **Finite normalization of a semigroup algebra.** Over an integrally closed domain `R`, for any
finitely generated submonoid `S` of a torsion-free abelian group `G` and any fraction ring `K` of
`R[S]`, the integral closure of `R[S]` in `K` is a finite `R[S]`-module. -/
theorem moduleFinite_integralClosure_fractionRing {R K : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG) [CommRing K]
    [Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] [IsFractionRing (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K] :
    Module.Finite (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (integralClosure (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) K) := by
  let := (mapDomainRingHom R
    (AddSubmonoid.inclusion (le_inf S.le_nsmulSaturation AddSubgroup.subset_closure))).toAlgebra
  have : Module.Finite (AddMonoidAlgebra R S)
      (AddMonoidAlgebra R
        ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid)) :=
    TauCeti.AddMonoidAlgebra.mapDomainRingHom_inclusion_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_finite hS R
  exact Module.Finite.equiv (nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquivIntegralClosure hS K).toLinearEquiv

/-- Over an integrally closed domain `R`, the semigroup algebra `R[S]` of any `NSMulSaturated`
submonoid `S` of a free abelian group `L` is integrally closed. -/
theorem isIntegrallyClosed_of_nsmulSaturated_of_free {R L : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [AddCommGroup L] [Module.Free ℤ L] {S : AddSubmonoid L}
    (hsat : S.NSMulSaturated) :
    IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) := by
  have : HasUniqueDiv L := .of_isTorsionFree ℤ L
  let _ : Algebra (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L) :=
    (mapDomainRingHom R S.subtype).toAlgebra
  have : IsIntegrallyClosedIn (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L) :=
    (S.isIntegrallyClosedIn_iff_nsmulSaturated R).mpr hsat
  have : FaithfulSMul (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L) :=
    (faithfulSMul_iff_algebraMap_injective _ _).mpr (mapDomain_injective S.subtype_injective)
  exact IsIntegrallyClosed.of_isIntegrallyClosed_of_isIntegrallyClosedIn
    (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) (AddMonoidAlgebra R L)

/-- **Normality of the saturation algebra.** Over an integrally closed domain `R`, the semigroup
algebra of `S.nsmulSaturation` for any submonoid `S` of a free abelian group `L` is integrally
closed. -/
instance isIntegrallyClosed_nsmulSaturation {R L : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [AddCommGroup L] [Module.Free ℤ L] {S : AddSubmonoid L} :
    IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R S.nsmulSaturation) :=
  isIntegrallyClosed_of_nsmulSaturated_of_free S.nsmulSaturated_nsmulSaturation

/-- Over an integrally closed domain `R`, the semigroup algebra of the saturation of `S` inside
`AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)` is integrally closed whenever `S` is finitely generated and `G`
is torsion-free. -/
theorem isIntegrallyClosed_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG) :
    IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R
      ↥(S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid)) := by
  have := hS.addSubgroupClosure
  exact IsIntegrallyClosed.of_equiv
    (mapDomainRingEquiv R S.nsmulSaturationInfClosureEquiv.symm)

/-- **Normality of a saturated semigroup algebra.** Over an integrally closed domain `R`, the
semigroup algebra `R[S]` of a finitely generated submonoid `S` of a torsion-free abelian group `G`
is integrally closed when `S` is saturated inside `AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)`. -/
theorem isIntegrallyClosed_of_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG)
    (hsat : S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid = S) :
    IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) :=
  hsat ▸ isIntegrallyClosed_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure hS

/-- Over an integrally closed domain `R`, the semigroup algebra `R[S]` of a finitely generated
`NSMulSaturated` submonoid `S` of a torsion-free abelian group `G` is integrally closed. -/
theorem isIntegrallyClosed_of_nsmulSaturated {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG)
    (hsat : S.NSMulSaturated) :
    IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) :=
  isIntegrallyClosed_of_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq hS <| by
    rw [AddSubmonoid.nsmulSaturation_eq_self hsat, inf_eq_left]
    exact AddSubgroup.subset_closure

/-- **Normality of a finitely generated semigroup algebra over a domain.** Over an integral domain
`R`, the semigroup algebra `R[S]` of a finitely generated submonoid `S` of a torsion-free abelian
group `G` is integrally closed if and only if `R` is integrally closed and `S` is saturated inside
`AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)`. -/
theorem isIntegrallyClosed_iff_isIntegrallyClosed_and_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq {R : Type*}
    [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG) :
    IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) ↔
      IsIntegrallyClosed R ∧
        S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid = S := by
  refine ⟨fun h => ⟨isIntegrallyClosed_of_addMonoidAlgebra (M := S),
    S.nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq R⟩, fun ⟨_, hsat⟩ => ?_⟩
  exact isIntegrallyClosed_of_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq hS hsat

/-- Variant of
`AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_iff_isIntegrallyClosed_and_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq`
phrased using `NSMulSaturated` on the pullback of `S` to `AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)`. -/
theorem isIntegrallyClosed_iff_isIntegrallyClosed_and_nsmulSaturated_comap_subtype_closure
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG) :
    IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) ↔
      IsIntegrallyClosed R ∧ (S.comap (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).subtype).NSMulSaturated :=
  (isIntegrallyClosed_iff_isIntegrallyClosed_and_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq hS).trans
    (and_congr_right' S.nsmulSaturated_comap_subtype_closure_iff.symm)

/-- **Normality of a finitely generated semigroup algebra over an integrally closed domain.** Over
an integrally closed domain `R` (for instance a field or `ℤ`), the semigroup algebra `R[S]` of a
finitely generated submonoid `S` of a torsion-free abelian group `G` is integrally closed if and
only if `S` is saturated inside `AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)`. -/
theorem isIntegrallyClosed_iff_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq_of_isIntegrallyClosed {R : Type*}
    [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G] {S : AddSubmonoid G}
    (hS : S.FG) :
    IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) ↔
      S.nsmulSaturation ⊓ (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).toAddSubmonoid = S := by
  simpa [‹IsIntegrallyClosed R›] using
    isIntegrallyClosed_iff_isIntegrallyClosed_and_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq (R := R) hS

/-- Variant of
`AddMonoidAlgebra.isIntegrallyClosed_iff_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq_of_isIntegrallyClosed`
phrased using `NSMulSaturated` on the pullback of `S` to `AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)`. -/
theorem isIntegrallyClosed_iff_nsmulSaturated_comap_subtype_closure_of_isIntegrallyClosed
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsIntegrallyClosed R] [HasUniqueDiv G]
    {S : AddSubmonoid G} (hS : S.FG) :
    IsIntegrallyClosed (AddMonoidAlgebra R S) ↔
      (S.comap (AddSubgroup.closure (S : Set G)).subtype).NSMulSaturated :=
  (isIntegrallyClosed_iff_nsmulSaturation_inf_closure_eq_of_isIntegrallyClosed hS).trans
    S.nsmulSaturated_comap_subtype_closure_iff.symm

end FractionFieldAndNormality

end AddMonoidAlgebra
